  "mix_notes": [
    "V014 was rejected after listening because the result still felt continuous and monotonous. V015 directly removes the sustained quality: every FM patch has a faster key-off release, the accompaniment is reduced to short stabs, and the lead occupies only 52 of 180 score frames.",
    "Keep the positively received V012 eight-note contour, but phrase it as three quick attacks, a separated F accent, a full breath, then a rising D-G-B-C answer. Syncopated pickups create motion instead of evenly spaced sustained notes.",
    "The mark-lock PCM cue occupies scene frames 118-129 (score 58-69) inside the deliberate musical breath. The answer resumes at score frame 72, two frames after that cue ends.",
    "Bass attacks only at score frames 0, 42, 72 and 102. Chord support is four short independent stabs at those same harmonic points; there is no pad or continuous low voice.",
    "Three additive FM crystal pings use E6/G6/C7 at score frames 26, 88 and 106, each 3-4 frames. They are short high-register color, not a sustained line.",
    "Finish the C-major landing by score frame 114. Keep score frames 118-144 clear for the sweep cue and frames 150-174 clear for the tail cue; PSG remains silent.",
    "Music starts at scene frame 60 after the 36-frame energy-rise cue and the stream ends at scene frame 240. Its 180-frame loop retains exact NTSC timing; the composed notes end well before the final PCM tail."
  ],
